/*
 * Sinonimia dictionary — ENGLISH.
 * This is a starter set that proves the multi-language setup works end to
 * end. It reuses pictograms already downloaded for the Spanish dictionary
 * (ARASAAC pictograms are language-neutral drawings), so no new images were
 * needed. Extend this file the same way js/data.es.js is extended — see the
 * field-by-field comments there. "situacion" must use the same shared keys:
 * "tramites", "salud", "vida-diaria", "finanzas", "vivienda", "trabajo", or
 * "legal" (see doc/en/SPEC.md; their on-screen labels live in js/i18n.js).
 *
 *  traduccion  -> OPTIONAL, same shape as in js/data.es.js: an object
 *                 keyed by other-language code whose values are ids (or
 *                 arrays of ids) of the equivalent entries in those
 *                 languages. The current mapping (scripts/.mapping.js
 *                 + scripts/inject-translations.js) only adds `traduccion`
 *                 on the ES side today — EN entries that need an ES
 *                 counterpart link are covered by the shared-pictogram
 *                 fallback in js/app.js. Add an EN-side `traduccion` only
 *                 if the fallback proves insufficient.
 */

